# Core and worker

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** [`packages/core/AGENTS.md`](../../packages/core/AGENTS.md) · root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)

## Do not

- Import React, Zustand, or DOM APIs in `@hd-wallet/core`
- Decrypt vault or hold secrets outside worker memory
- Change vault formats, derivation paths, or worker API contracts without an approved high-risk plan
- Skip focused Vitest for crypto/vault/signing/persistence changes
- Put new chain logic in React; use `packages/core/src/chains/`
- Use `@/` imports in core; use relative `.js` imports
- Branch vault existence on `loadVaultMetadata().hasVault` alone in new code

Treat edits under `packages/core` and `apps/web/src/workers/` as high-risk escalation triggers.

## Vault existence reads

For existence checks and UI routing reads, use `getVaultMetadata()` or `hasVault()` from `vault/metadata.ts`. Reserve `loadVaultMetadata()` for storage internals. Keep `persistVault()` gated on reconciled metadata.

## Pattern anchors

### BAD

```ts
// packages/core — forbidden UI dependency
import { useState } from "react";
import { useSessionStore } from "@hd-wallet/stores";
```

### GOOD

```ts
// packages/core — pure crypto API, relative .js import
import { decryptVault } from "../vault/cipher.js";

export async function unlockVault(password: string, vault: EncryptedVault) {
  return decryptVault(password, vault);
}
```

## Tests

- Run: `pnpm --filter @hd-wallet/core test`
- Cover: KDF, encrypt/decrypt round-trip, derivation vectors, lock/unlock, wrong password
- Add or update Vitest when changing `vault/metadata.ts`, `vault/storage.ts`, or `vault/vault-service.ts`
